{"type": "lesson", "id": "LES-2026-06-10-qa-attribution-method", "date": "2026-06-10", "lesson": "Never log a landing winner whose arms use different attribution methods: /try (tbs_* cohort) vs home (first-pageview pathname, known to mis-credit value-first signups to /) is not a comparison; re-derive both arms under one method before any beats/loses lesson.", "evidence": "QA calls lens 2026-06-10 caught LES try-value-first drafted at med on mismatched arms; downgraded to low and reframed.", "confidence": "high", "tags": ["qa", "measurement", "cro"], "source_pred": null}
{"type": "lesson", "id": "LES-2026-06-10-qa-denominator-splice", "date": "2026-06-10", "lesson": "Name numerator event, denominator cohort, and window for every rate written into the OS: today spliced a spine numerator onto an aha denominator (9/54; real: 11 lifetime pricing reach, 9/125 spine) and quoted lifetime tryon-rate cohorts (Meta 32% vs Direct 57%) as last-7d model-rate evidence.", "evidence": "QA numbers lens 2026-06-10, refutations on CC ranks 3-4.", "confidence": "high", "tags": ["qa", "numbers"], "source_pred": null}
{"type": "lesson", "id": "LES-2026-06-10-qa-pred-metric-compliance", "date": "2026-06-10", "lesson": "Citing a QA lesson in a prediction rationale while keeping the metric it forbids is acknowledgment-without-compliance: reject any prediction bound to a flight-cumulative or rolling aggregate when the action shipped mid-window; hold the bet until a clean cohort metric exists.", "evidence": "QA calls lens 2026-06-10 refuted PRED-try-paid-default (flight-cumulative cpl, autopilot confound, rollout premise overstated); prediction held, not logged.", "confidence": "high", "tags": ["qa", "predictions"], "source_pred": null}
{"type": "lesson", "id": "LES-2026-06-10-qa-run-provenance", "date": "2026-06-10", "lesson": "Persist what you act on and what you cite: empty run logs made the coachmarks 100%-flag and the paid-default rollout unauditable, and live-read ad-set figures (imps/PV, 24h CPL) were unverifiable; record executed actions in run-*.json and either persist live-read figures or do not cite them.", "evidence": "QA boundary lens 2026-06-10: run-2026-06-08/10.json effectively empty; $24.42 not derivable (history gives $23.64); /toddler 800/10/0 in no persisted source.", "confidence": "high", "tags": ["qa", "process"], "source_pred": null}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-10-price-ask-checkout","date":"2026-06-10","action":"Run price-ask test: manually onboard 5 Kids and 5 Swim founders this week, walk each to try-on, ask for card; combined with Convert C4 paid-ask emails reaching first-wave aha users around Jun 13","linked":"CC-rank-1","metric":"payment_rate","baseline":10,"predicted":13,"horizon_days":15,"due":"2026-06-25","rationale":"Two parallel mechanisms: (1) 10 founders hand-walked to try-on, conservative 30% checkout rate = 3 new starters; (2) Convert C4 fires for aha users in the flow since Jun 6, adding further intent. Combined: 10 to 13. Distinct from PRED-2026-06-05-post-aha-email (baseline 8, email-only, current count already at 10). Moot if price-ask test not started by Jun 17.","scoring":"checkout_started reach >= 13 by Jun 25; moot if price-ask test not started by Jun 17","status":"resolved","actual":6,"verdict":"miss","resolved_date":"2026-06-17","lesson_id":"LES-2026-06-17-price-ask-moot"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-10-qa-live-vs-curated-funnel","date":"2026-06-10","lesson":"Always read data.js .live.funnel (live HogQL, updated daily) not .funnelCurated (cached snapshot, updated Jun 3): the cached section showed 64 signups/30 tryons/8 checkouts while the live section showed 125/54/10; nearly overwrote correct commandCenter status text with wrong numbers.","evidence":"QA catch Jun 10: live.funnel.stages checkout all=10, tryon all=54, signup all=125 vs funnelCurated 8/30/64. The commandCenter items correctly use live figures. Edits to rank-2 and rank-3 were held after QA.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","process","numbers"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-kids-pixel-swap","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"A creative swap to a new landing URL requires pixel verification before routing paid traffic: the Jun-8 /toddler→/try-kids swap produced an unaudited signal of 0 PageViews on 12 clicks, potentially $16/day burning blind on the top-spend segment.","evidence":"Campaigns read-agent live-read 2026-06-11 (unaudited -- not in history.jsonl or data.js); autopilot TRACKING_ISSUE flag on Kids adset.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","paid","meta","pixel","tracking"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-qa-adsegment-unpersisted","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"Never cite ad-set-level figures (segment CPL, per-adset PageViews, impression counts) as facts unless they appear verbatim in data.js or history.jsonl. data.js explicitly warns these are not persisted; live-read figures must be written to a persisted record before they can be cited in decisions.","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-11: Swim CPL $0.51 absent from all sources (nearest $2.22); Kids 0-PageViews claim sourced from live read only; data.js commandCenter rank 5 body explicitly states 'ad-set-level counts are not persisted'.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","paid","meta","numbers"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-qa-exp-snapshot-vs-live","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"The OS-SIGNUP-GOOGLE 'after' field in data.js (44.7%, 105/235) is a frozen May-27 cohort snapshot, not the current signup_completion_rate. Use live.funnel intent→signup d7 for current scoring (52.8% as of Jun 11).","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-11: d7 modal intent=106, signup=56 → 52.8%, exceeds the 50% prediction target. 44.7% is a stale cohort field.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","signup","measurement","predictions"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-qa-funnel-rank","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"Under a first-paying-customer goal, upstream funnel gates (activation) must rank above downstream optimizations (/try UX, pixel attribution) that can only affect users who already passed the upstream gate.","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-11: 43% activation (54% rolling) means 57% of signups never reach the paywall; ranking category-fix above activation gap is structurally backwards.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","prioritization"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-qa-pred-early-flag","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"When a prediction's current value is below the pre-intervention baseline (not just below the target), flag it as a directional miss immediately regardless of the due date -- the trajectory itself is informative under short goal timelines.","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-11: PRED-2026-06-03-activate-flow target 75, baseline 69, current 54 -- below baseline, not just below target. 13 days to due, 19 days to end-June goal.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions","process"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-kids-pixel-not-a-bug","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"The Kids '/try-kids 0 PageViews' alarm is a Meta-side reporting artifact (ad-block asymmetry), NOT a code bug: PostHog independently recorded 122 paid pageviews / 101 people on /try-kids in 14d. SPA rewrite + base pixel + no consent gate all verified correct. Reverting to /toddler would not help (identical architecture). Real fix is server-side Meta CAPI, a Jason build.","evidence":"PostHog $pageview on /try-kids: 135/106 (14d), 122 utm_source=meta; vercel.json /(.*)→index.html; index.html:31-32 base pixel.","confidence":"high","tags":["paid","meta","pixel","tracking","diagnosis"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-activation-mixshift-confirmed","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"The activation decline is CONFIRMED mix-shift, not a product regression: paid activates 44% vs direct 66% (30d, signup→model_generated), and paid's share of signups rose from 50% (30d) to 73% (7d), dragging the blend down. Direct still activates 48-66% so the product step is intact. Fix is traffic quality + the live Activate flow, not emergency product work.","evidence":"PostHog activation-by-channel 2026-06-11: meta/paid 44.0%(50) vs direct 66.0%(47) 30d; paid share 50→73% across 30d→7d windows.","confidence":"high","tags":["funnel","activation","paid","diagnosis"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-purchase-wiring-ok","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"purchase_completed wiring is correct end-to-end (Stripe success_url=/account?success=true → AccountPage fires track, keyed to user.id matching the funnel person). 0 fires ≈ 0 real completed purchases (10 started, 0 paid), not a tracking bug; confirm in Stripe. Robustness gap: client-side fire is ad-blockable; bulletproof fix is server-side capture from the existing checkout.session.completed webhook (no server PostHog client yet, so a Jason build).","evidence":"stripe.routes.ts:74, stripe.service.ts:109/139, AccountPage.tsx:44-52, analytics.ts:27; no posthog-node in apps/server.","confidence":"high","tags":["funnel","payment","tracking","diagnosis"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-meta-dark","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"Meta ads went dark: $0 spend + 0 impressions across all 4 segments for 3+ days (Jun 13-15), and the dashboard's $8.33 CPL is a frozen lifetime average (241.52/29), not a live read. A 'Live' status with a flat CPL can mask zero delivery — always check incremental spend, not the CPL tile.","evidence":"history.jsonl spend_lifetime frozen 241.52 Jun13-15, cpl 8.33 + signups_meta 29 identical; autopilot plan_actions=[] '0 impressions' every cycle.","confidence":"high","tags":["paid","meta","delivery","ops"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-qa-metric-mislabel","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"Only cite an X%→Y% before/after when both numbers label the SAME metric: a draft claimed the Jun-12 overhaul moved signup→model 41→43, but 41 is the signup→activation goal tile and 43 is the open→signup modal leak, neither is signup→model (67% reach). Grep the exact values and confirm the metric before asserting a movement.","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-15: 41% and 43% tag different data.js tiles; daily models/signups ratio too noisy to source a clean before/after.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","numbers","measurement"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-qa-window-zero","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"A '0 in the last N days' claim must be checked across the whole window, not the tail: 'payment_rate 10→6, 0 checkouts in 10 days' was wrong, the recent series is 7→6 (10 was the prediction baseline) and checkouts were 1 on Jun 8 and 1 on Jun 10, only Jun 13-15 were zero.","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-15: history.jsonl payment_rate Jun7-15=7,7,7,7,7,6,6,6,6; checkouts Jun8=1, Jun10=1.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","numbers"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-qa-confound-vs-fail","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"Do not conflate 'confounded/unidentifiable' with 'failed': when channel mix-shift confounds activation, a shipped overhaul's effect is unmeasurable, not zero. Asserting both 'it's mix-shift' and 'the overhaul didn't move it' is incoherent, the honest call is 'effect unreadable, bind a clean before/after.'","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-15 on the activation-gap item; numbers lens confirmed no clean pre/post series exists.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","measurement","predictions"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-qa-source-pin","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"QA skeptics must verify against the run's actual sources (data.js + history.jsonl), not a same-named MCP graph: a skeptic this run read the 'marketingos' MCP (an unrelated hiring graph) and could not verify anything, voiding its data-dependent verdicts. Pin the file paths in the skeptic brief and tell it not to use MCP workspaces.","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-15 returned 'workspace is CodeSignal hiring graph, n=0'; its logic points held but data claims were void.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","process"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-12-channel-quality-gap","date":"2026-06-12","lesson":"Direct/organic users convert to checkout at 13.4% (9/67 signups) vs Meta users at 1.4% (1/69 signups): a 10x downstream quality gap. 9 of 10 all-time checkouts came from the Direct channel. For the first paying customer, prioritize manual outreach to high-intent Direct/LinkedIn cohort (Wave 1/2 referrals) over cold Meta signups.","evidence":"live.channels.attribution Jun 12: Direct 596 users, 67 signups, 39 tryons, 9 checkouts; Meta 916 users, 69 signups, 21 tryons, 1 checkout. N=10 checkouts total, so treat as med confidence.","confidence":"med","tags":["funnel","paid","meta","channels","conversion"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-12-studio-rageclicks","date":"2026-06-12","action":"Escalate the /studio rage-click cluster to Jason as a concrete product UX bug report (33 users, 70 events, recurring daily: Jun 7=8, Jun 11=7) and ship the specific control fix","linked":"CC-rank-4","metric":"activation_rate","baseline":53,"predicted":58,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-06-26","rationale":"The /studio UX barrier is persistent and daily, independent of channel mix-shift: 24% of studio entrants rage-click. The mix-shift diagnosis (LES-2026-06-11-activation-mixshift-confirmed) explains the blended-rate decline but not the daily rage-click pattern. Fixing the blocked control should recover some non-activators. Conservative 5pp call: baseline 53% (75/141 spine signup→model_generated Jun 12). Moot if no product fix shipped by due date.","scoring":"spine model_generated/signup % post-fix vs Jun 12 baseline of 53% (75/141); require >=14d post-fix cohort data; moot if fix not shipped by due date","status":"open"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-meta-dark-RETRACTED","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"RETRACTS LES-2026-06-15-meta-dark. Meta was NOT dark. The Meta API shows healthy daily spend Jun 8-14 ($17-58/day, ~$277/wk, 27k impressions Jun 14). The OS's Meta feed went STALE around Jun 12 (build.py carried $241.52/29 signups forward), and a frozen lifetime CPL ($8.33) was misread as $0 incremental spend. Lesson: verify a 'something stopped' alarm against the SOURCE (Meta API / Ads Manager) before raising it, a flat dashboard number is more often a broken feed than a real outage.","evidence":"ads_get_ad_entities account 3682177848625068 last_7d daily: Jun8 $57.96/2900imp ... Jun14 $41.68/26979imp; OS data.js spend frozen 241.52 since Jun 12.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","paid","meta","measurement","process"]}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-16-aha-cta-rework","date":"2026-06-16","action":"Rewrite AHA flow B1 and B2 CTAs with a direct action link and concrete value line, replacing the zero-click current CTA (B1: 11 recipients, 36.4% open, 0 clicks; B2: 9 recipients, 33.3% open, 0 clicks)","linked":"CC-rank-2","metric":"payment_rate","baseline":6,"predicted":8,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-06-30","rationale":"Both deployed AHA messages have strong opens (36.4% B1, 33.3% B2) and 0 clicks across 20 combined recipient-opens. Opens confirm deliverability and intent; 0 clicks is a copy or link failure. If 2-3 of 11 B1 readers click to /studio and 1-2 start checkout, payment_rate reaches 8% (12+ checkouts on 155+ signups). Window closing: users cycle out of the flow. Conservative call on thin sample (9 all-time checkouts). Conditional on rework shipping by Jun 21.","scoring":"payment_rate >= 8 by 2026-06-30; spine denominator 155+; moot if B1/B2 CTAs not rewritten by 2026-06-21","status":"open"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-16-qa-modal-d7-drift","date":"2026-06-16","lesson":"The d7 modal completion rate drifts as the 7-day window rolls: the Jun-15 CC rank-8 status cited 52.8% but today's live data shows 34/71 = 47.9%, which is below the PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link target of 50%. Never carry a prior d7 figure forward; recompute from live.funnel.stages d7 intent and signup counts each run.","evidence":"live.funnel.stages d7: intent=71, signup=34 -> 34/71=47.9%. Jun-15 CC rank-8 status cited 52.8% from a different d7 window cut.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","signup","measurement","predictions"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-17-price-ask-moot","date":"2026-06-17","lesson":"When a price-ask test has a moot condition ('moot if not started by date X') and that date arrives without the test running, resolve the prediction as a miss rather than leaving it open: the causal mechanism was never activated, but the outcome is still real and the ledger must close. The next action is not a fresh prediction of the same bet -- it is a narrower, more concrete outreach to the highest-intent contacts already in the funnel.","evidence":"PRED-2026-06-10-price-ask-checkout moot condition fired Jun 17: test not started despite being rank-1 for 7 days. payment_rate stayed at 6 (baseline stated in prediction was 10). Resolved miss.","confidence":"high","tags":["predictions","process"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-10-price-ask-checkout"}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-17-checkout-outreach","date":"2026-06-17","action":"Personal 1:1 outreach to each of the 10 Direct-channel checkout starters before Jun 20; confirm their Stripe dropout reason, offer concierge onboarding, close the first purchase","linked":"CC-rank-1","metric":"payment_rate","baseline":6,"predicted":8,"horizon_days":7,"due":"2026-06-24","rationale":"10 people have started checkout (9 from Direct, 1 from Meta) and 0 have paid. These are the highest-intent contacts in the funnel: they saw pricing, clicked through to Stripe, and stopped. A personal email asking what got in the way is the surest path to the first paying customer. Direct converts to checkout at 14.1% (10/71 signups) vs Meta 1.2% (1/81 signups). Even 1 completion plus 2 more new checkouts = 13/159 = 8.2% payment_rate. Conditional: requires reaching at least 5 of the 10 checkout starters before Jun 20.","scoring":"payment_rate >= 8 OR paying_customers >= 1 by 2026-06-24; moot if no personal outreach to checkout starters before Jun 20","status":"open"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-17-qa-c4-timing","date":"2026-06-17","lesson":"A 0% open rate on a triggered email may be a timing artifact rather than a deliverability failure when the recipient count is small and the send is recent: if the 7-day delay window elapsed within the last 24-48h, the emails may simply not have had time to be opened. Verify send timestamps against the trigger event date before treating 0% open as actionable. C1's 100% open is a different cohort (different trigger window) and cannot serve as a control.","evidence":"QA Jun 17: C4 Convert flow (Day 7 paid-ask) shows 0% open across 5 recipients. C1 same flow shows 100% open on 5 different recipients. Flagged as high-sev in CC rank 4 but conditioned on Klaviyo delivery log verification through Jun 20.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","lifecycle","email","measurement"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-18-modal-ceiling","date":"2026-06-18","lesson":"Removing magic-link lifted modal completion from 33% to ~45% (all-time) but not to the 50% target: the ceiling appears to be in-modal OAuth friction (desktop lags mobile, consent screen adds a step), not the inbox round-trip that was the baseline culprit. The next modal fix requires reducing in-modal friction, not removing more options.","evidence":"PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link resolved miss Jun 18: d7 completion 28/61=45.9%, all-time post-May-27 132/293=45.1%, both below 50% target. magic_link_requested=0 for 14+ days confirms removal held; gains are real (+12pp from 33%) but short of target.","confidence":"med","tags":["funnel","signup","measurement","predictions"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link"}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-18-try-generate-gap","date":"2026-06-18","action":"Fix the /try garment→generate 46% drop: make the Generate button unmissable after a garment is added (more prominent CTA, load-state feedback, or inline 'Now generate your try-on' prompt on the garment-added screen)","linked":"CC-rank-4","metric":"home_signup_pct","baseline":10.1,"predicted":12.5,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-07-02","rationale":"510 /try viewers → 199 category selected → 169 garment added → only 91 clicked Generate (46% drop, 78 high-intent garment-adders lost). Recovering 30% of those 78 at current downstream generate→signup rate (57.6%, 53/92) adds ~13 signers, lifting /try view→signup from 10.1% to ~12.5%. Wave 3 paid traffic starts today, growing the denominator fast and making this testable within 14d. Calibration thin: single day this alarm appeared. Moot if no UI fix shipped by Jul 2.","scoring":"resolve on post-fix /try tbs cohort view→signup rate vs 10.1% baseline; NOT blended home_signup_pct (which tracks homepage, not /try); require >=7d post-fix tbs* data; Wave 3 confound: if paid quality drops, rate may fall even with the fix; score vs cohort not time-series. Moot if fix not shipped by Jul 2.","status":"open"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-18-qa-generate-gap-distinct","date":"2026-06-18","lesson":"The /try funnel has two separate leaks that require distinct fixes: (1) category-selection drop (39% pass-through, affects all /try visitors) and (2) garment→generate drop (54% pass-through among higher-intent garment-adders, 46% loss at highest intent). QA today refuted a draft that merged both into the category fix: different steps, different user states, different root causes. Rank them separately.","evidence":"QA Jun 18: data.js funnelSuggestions surfaces garment→generate drop (91/169=53.8%) as a new distinct alarm; CC rank-7 category fix (199/510=39%) predates it; PRED-2026-06-09-tbs-category-fix covers the category step only. Added CC rank-4 for the generate drop.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","try","process"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-18-try-generate-gap"}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-19-onboarding-model-filter","date":"2026-06-19","action":"Pre-filter the onboarding model gallery to ~5-8 matches based on the user's Q1 segment answer (kids/swim/womenswear), eliminating the cold browse of 50+ models","linked":"CC-rank-3","metric":"activation_rate","baseline":51,"predicted":57,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-07-03","rationale":"63 of 77 recent signups (14d since Jun 4) answered all 3 onboarding questions but only 29 picked a model (38% pass-through, 54% drop at model selection). After model pick, 28/29 generated (97%), so model selection is almost the entire loss, not generation. The questionnaire already knows the segment; surfacing 5-8 matching models instead of 50+ cold eliminates choice paralysis at the pinch point. Recovering 30% of the 34 who bailed at model pick in the cohort would recover ~10 activations. Conservative 6pp call on thin sample (14d, n=77). All-time spine (82/162=51%) is the more stable baseline. Moot if not shipped by Jul 3.","scoring":"resolve on onboarding Q3-to-model-pick pass-through rate post-fix vs 29/63=46% baseline; activation_rate (spine) is directional; require >=14d post-fix data; moot if fix not shipped by Jul 3","status":"open"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-19-qa-c4-stale-status","date":"2026-06-19","lesson":"The commandCenter C4 status ('12 recipients, 0% open') was stale at write time: live.lifecycle in the same data.js showed C4 at 20 recipients, 20.0% open, 0 clicks. Deliverability was fine; the problem is CTA copy, not spam. A stale CC status inverted the diagnostic (spam vs copy), causing a wrong investigation brief. Verify lifecycle stats directly from live.lifecycle on each reasoning pass, not from a prior CC status.","evidence":"QA Jun 19: data.js live.lifecycle C4=20 recipients/20% open vs CC rank-6 status citing 12/0%. CC was written before the Klaviyo pull refreshed. The 0% open alarm was incorrect; investigation priority and direction changed on QA.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","lifecycle","email","process"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-22-cta-rework","date":"2026-06-22","action":"Rework Convert C2-C5 + AHA B1/B2 paid-ask CTAs to one concrete action line plus a direct /studio-or-checkout link; current CTAs draw 0 clicks across 105 (Convert) + 24 (AHA) recipients despite 20-42% opens.","linked":"CC-rank-2","metric":"email_click","baseline":0.0,"predicted":5.0,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-07-06","rationale":"Aggregate email_click has been 0.0 for 5+ straight days while email_open holds 31-33% -- a pure CTA failure, not deliverability or timing. One concrete action + a direct link should produce nonzero clicks. Conservative target (5%) given thin calibration (0.33, n=3). Contingent on the live-flow edit shipping (escalate-gated); moot if unshipped by due date.","status":"open"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-22-qa-try-data-location","date":"2026-06-22","lesson":"The tbs /try funnel numbers (category pass-through, garment->generate drop) live in live.meta.funnelSuggestions and the experiments/learning prose, NOT in live.funnel.stages -- so the Funnel read-agent (which reads only live.funnel) will miss them and a date-stamp of 'not in today's data.js' is wrong. Before stamping any /try metric as absent or stale, grep the WHOLE data.js including funnelSuggestions.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jun 22: funnelSuggestions[0].evidence = '622 viewed -> 230 category -> 198 garment -> 105 Generate' dated Jun 22 'unchanged from last cycle'; I had labeled ranks 7 & 9 'last measured Jun 19, not in data.js' -- wrong, corrected.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","data-source"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-22-qa-log-clean-baseline","date":"2026-06-22","lesson":"A clean, observable-now baseline (e.g. email_click=0 across 129 recipients) should be logged as a prediction at decision/queue time, not deferred to ship-time -- 'log the PRED when it ships' risks losing the pre-state and lets the top fix-lever run unbet. Logging a bet does not require shipping the fix; mark it moot-if-unshipped.","evidence":"QA calls skeptic Jun 22: the new #2 lever (Convert C2-C5 rework) had a crisp 0-click baseline but no PRED; the roadmap deferred it. Logged PRED-2026-06-22-cta-rework in response.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","ledger","process"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-22-cta-rework"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-22-qa-checkout-window","date":"2026-06-22","lesson":"The checkout-starter count differs by view/window: same-user spine = 10, reach (all) = 11, d30 reach = 5. Always cite which view a checkout figure comes from. A skeptic refuted '10' as '7', but 7 was an OLD status's d30 figure, not the live spine -- the live spine count (10) stands. Reconcile to live.funnel.spine, and never let a stale CC status's number override the live spine.","evidence":"data.js live.funnel.spine 'Started checkout' count=10; stages.checkout.counts {d7:1,d30:5,all:11}; the disputed '7' matched no live value (it was a prior status's d30 reach).","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","numbers"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-22-meta-feed-rootcause","date":"2026-06-22","lesson":"The Meta feed 'froze' at $241.52 not because the feed broke but because the autopilot's lifetime pull was hardcoded to ONE campaign (CAMPAIGN_ID, the Jun-2 relaunch) while Ablo spend had spread across 3 campaigns (paused May-20 original $512/25, Jun-3 LP-test $460/52 ACTIVE, relaunch $241/29). Real lifetime is $1,332/111/$12.01 CPL. Fixed in autopilot lib/meta.py + run_cycle.py: lifetime report now paginates all campaigns, name-matches 'Ablo' (excludes 200+ unrelated 'AI .' junk campaigns in the shared ad account), sums via date_preset=maximum; the campaign the autopilot ACTS on is unchanged. Heuristic: when a campaign-scoped metric looks frozen, first check whether spend moved to a sibling campaign the scope misses, before assuming a broken feed or dark ads. This is the true root cause behind LES-2026-06-15-meta-dark.","evidence":"meta.lifetime_insights_ablo() live: 9 adsets $1332.89/111 regs; account-level 30d showed 3 Ablo campaigns + ~$140 AI-junk; dry-run regenerated LATEST.md to $1332.89/111/$12.01.","confidence":"high","tags":["campaigns","data-integrity","autopilot"],"source_pred":""}
